          "payload": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "For undergraduate students at UAE University, excluding those in the College of Medicine and Health Sciences, attendance is mandatory for all registered course classes, practicals, seminars, and examinations; missing 15% or more of class meetings leads to a failing grade for absences (FA).\n\nFor undergraduates, excluding the College of Medicine and Health Sciences: Absences approved by the Dean within the semester can result in Administrative Withdrawal with a grade of AW instead of failure, and such Dean-approved absences are not counted toward the 15% absence limit, with a general waiver cap of 12.5% of total class meeting hours.\n\nFor undergraduates, excluding the College of Medicine and Health Sciences: Students are responsible for tracking their attendance through the e-Services system, and the attendance rule excludes allowances such as UAE representation at national events, which is separately waived and not part of the 15% absence limit.",
