                "lastVerified": "2026-11-04",
                "sourceSection": "Scope; Procedures section9 Attendance; effective12Aug2018",
                "sourceVersion": "Official public source accessed 2026-11-04; access date is not policy effective date",
                "evidenceText": "The published UAEU Undergraduate Registration and Enrollment procedures AE-03, effective12August2018, exclude the College of Medicine and Health Sciences. Section9 requires attendance at all registered course classes, practicals, seminars and examinations. Missing15% of class meetings results in FA (Fail for Absences). A valid reason approved by the Dean in the semester of the absence permits Administrative Withdrawal and gradeAW instead. Dean-waived absences are not counted toward that15% requirement, and the stated general waiver cap is12.5% of total class meeting hours. Students track attendance in e-Services. The document separately waives UAE representation at events of national interest; do not turn the general cap into an exception-free rule. This source does not establish the separate Medicine attendance rule."
              }
            ],
